  "displayName": "The Ashland Rim",
  "subtitle": "Grey ash at the edge of the Wasting, where the Ash-Walkers hold the Eastern Ridge",
  "canonStatus": "CANON-EXPANDED",
  "canonNote": "Canon (book1 ch.20): the Ash-Walkers live along the Wasting and fight the Weave-Eaters with Salt of the First Sea; Chieftain Grohl and Mother Vane, the Salt-Speaker, lead them from an enclave in the deep caves of the Eastern Ridge, across a plain of petrified ash. The Cult of Ash (Torvyn Embercloak, Vorn) and its iron-wired bone masks are canon (book1 ch.10, series_bible.md); the purple tear is the later House of Ash's symbol (series_bible.md), used here early (GAME-ONLY). The books also call Torvyn's cultists 'Ashwalkers'; the game keeps the Ash-Walkers of ch.20 and the Cult of Ash apart. The canon Ashlands take their full form after the Spoke fires (series_bible.md), so this pre-erasure rim is PROVISIONAL. GAME-ONLY: the zone's name and its roads to the Peaks and Oakhaven, the cult shrine's location, Cinderfold, the old ribcage, the ash hounds, the brood, and all placement.",
